Description:
    Provides an automated, reproducible pipeline for gating multi-colour flow
    cytometry data stored in FCS files.  Starting from raw FCS data, the
    package applies compensation and Gating-ML transformations, then trains
    a hierarchy of gates (singlets, cells, threshold gates on one or two
    channels, polygons) on pooled training samples and applies it to every
    sample.  Thresholds are calculated from the data by a Gaussian mixture
    crossover, a symmetric tail, a density valley, or Otsu's method, or are
    replicated from another gate or a reference population.  Gating models
    are read and written as Honeychrome '.agmodel' files, so models move
    between this package and the Honeychrome application.  Population counts,
    fractions and marker medians are exported as tidy CSV files, with figures
    of every gate as applied and of the differences between groups.
    Instrument-specific parameter profiles are provided for the BD
    FACSymphony and LSRFortessa, Cytek Aurora, and Sony ID7000 cytometers.
